text:
elaine: quick UX review pls — proposing a compact credentials row (dense) for the dashboard. Inline CTAs: Rotate (primary) + Revoke (secondary under kebab). Main concerns: revoke CTA placement & affordance, clipboard announce when "show secret" is used, and soft-undo timing for revokes. Screenshot: https://img.redwood/mock/cred-row-compact.png

jmiller: +1 on compact if we keep clear affordances. My take: make Rotate primary (most common), put Revoke in overflow to reduce destructive clicks. Revoke should still show immediate modal + undo toast (10–30s).

sasha: UX nits — spacing looks tight for keyboard focus ring. If we go dense, ensure 44–48px tap targets for mobile. Also empty-state needs a prominent centered "Create key" CTA — current left-aligned feels lost.

kevin: accessibility notes: use aria-live="polite" for general toasts. For clipboard copy, I usually do an assertive announce for screen readers: but careful — assertive interrupts. Suggest: polite for success toast, assertive for errors. Revoke confirmation should use role="alertdialog" and move focus into the dialog.

elaine: good call. For the clipboard behaviour we want immediate feedback but not too jarring. Maybe assertive only when the copy fails. Otherwise polite is fine. Also consider a visible inline label: "Secret copied" + screen reader announcement.

aria-bot: accessibility-linter: suggestion: prefer aria-live="polite" on toasts. Only use assertive for critical alerts. Ensure focus management on dialogs and that the revoke button uses aria-describedby for the warning copy.

ops-kate: ops perspective: if we implement soft-undo for revoke, what's the window? Users have asked for longer windows (60s) in support tickets. We currently treat revoked keys as 'disabled' in metadata immediately but still accept requests for 30s to allow autoscale rollbacks.

jmiller: 30s seems like a reasonable default for safety and rollback. Make it org-configurable (admins can extend to 60s). In the UI add a microcopy on the revoke CTA: "Revoke (undo available for 30s)" or tooltip.

elaine: agreed — I'll make 30s default and add org setting in the admin page. Updating mocks: will move Revoke to kebab and keep Rotate as visible primary. Also increasing row height slightly to preserve focus outlines.

elaine: quick code sketch for clipboard announce I'm going to include in the spec (very small):
```html
<button id=\"show-secret\">Show secret</button>
<div id=\"toast\" aria-live=\"polite\" aria-atomic=\"true\"></div>
<script>
document.getElementById('show-secret').addEventListener('click', ()=>{
  navigator.clipboard.writeText(secret).then(()=>{
    document.getElementById('toast').textContent = 'Secret copied to clipboard';
  }, ()=>{
    document.getElementById('toast').textContent = 'Failed to copy secret';
  });
});
</script>
```

jmiller: that looks good — add visually-hidden text for SRs if you want assertive behaviour on errors: `<span class=\"sr-only\" aria-live=\"assertive\">Failed to copy</span>`

sasha: tiny copy suggestion: instead of "Secret copied to clipboard" use "Secret copied" — shorter and fits the toast width better.

elaine: noted. I'll update mocks and the spec doc. Thanks all — I'll post the new frames in #design once done. :sparkles:
